31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
36,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that bulk earth-moving is risky because of clay subsoil and slippage, and only two firms are tendering. Also, only the southern ground can be hoarded in stages while keeping the park open.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"That sounds like a bit of a headache, Minato! It seems we need to be very careful about where we dig and how we phase the work if we want to avoid a total mess.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit worrying, isn't it? I found that while our water-based works from years ago have held up beautifully, the paved areas have struggled and many of our young trees sadly perished due to poor aftercare.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It seems we have a significant gap in our internal capacity. The groundskeeping staff has shrunk from eighteen to seven, meaning we rely heavily on bought-in services for specialized care.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The ground is fighting us. Drainage issues are doubling and the heat is oppressive. Plus, people aren't wandering; they're using the park as a direct, firm corridor to the tram stop. We can't ignore the actual behavior of the site.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, if people just want a firm path to the tram, maybe we shouldn't change the center too much. @Shizue, it's sad about the trees. I wonder if a plan with less digging would be safer?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, you're on the right track! I've discovered that maintaining greenery and water features costs triple what hard surfaces do. With our budget and shrinking staff, a ""lush"" plan might be a financial nightmare.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, that is a very important point. If we cannot afford to water the trees we already have, we must be very careful about adding more. We should choose something that truly lasts.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, your findings on costs align with my concerns about staffing. With only seven staff members left, we cannot sustain a high-maintenance landscape without relying on expensive external contracts or unreliable labor.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. We have a site that's overheating, flooding, and being used as a shortcut. If we pick a plan that ignores the drainage crisis or blocks the main thoroughfare, we're just designing a failure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I think we should avoid anything that requires a lot of bulk digging in the center, since that's where the slippage risk is and where people walk. Maybe something in the south would be better?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"I'm with you, Minato! If we keep the heavy lifting to the south and avoid high-maintenance greenery, we might actually save some money for once. Let's look for something practical and affordable.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree with you both. It seems we must be honest about our limits. A plan that mimics nature but lacks the care to sustain it would be a tragedy for the community.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"We must also consider the human element. I found that we have existing volunteer groups for habitat and sports. If we choose a plan that aligns with their current skills, we can offset our staffing shortage.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, that's a useful lever. But let's be rational: we have a drainage crisis and a heat island. If we don't address the water and the temperature, the volunteers will just be managing a swamp or a furnace.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I agree with Shunichi. We need to fix the water and heat problems, but we must do it carefully. I hope the plans have a way to help the drainage without too much risky digging.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm starting to think a ""less is more"" approach is our best bet. Let's hope the candidates include something that balances the drainage needs with a budget that won't make me scream in three years!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I feel we are all seeing the same truth now. We must be gentle with the land and honest about our ability to care for it, lest we create another sad memory.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. We need a solution that is sustainable not just environmentally, but operationally. A plan that leverages our existing volunteer strengths while remaining manageable for our limited staff is the only rational choice.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's stop the sentimentality. We need a plan that solves the drainage, handles the heat, respects the tram-stop traffic, and doesn't require a miracle budget. If it doesn't check those boxes, it's useless. Let's see the candidates.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think we should avoid A and B. A has too many trees and B is in the center where digging is risky and people walk. D helps drainage, but is it too much digging?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, A is a total budget trap! Dense trees and gravel paths mean triple the upkeep costs. B is paved, which is cheaper, but if it blocks the tram route, it's a disaster. I'm leaning toward C or D.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I am very concerned about A; we have already seen how our young trees suffer without care. D seems most promising, as our previous water-based works have remained strong and beautiful over the years.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I agree with Shizue. D aligns with our existing habitat volunteer group, which helps our staffing shortage. C is in the south, which is safer for construction, but D addresses the drainage crisis Shunichi mentioned.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"A is a maintenance nightmare and B is a heat-trap that ignores the drainage crisis. C is safe, but D actually solves the flooding and heat issues while respecting the ground's nature. D is the only rational choice.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I agree with everyone. D seems to solve the most problems and fits what we've learned. If the water works have lasted before, then D is the safest and most helpful choice for the park.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"I'm sold on D! It handles the drainage, and since Shizue mentioned water-based works last, it's a safer bet than a forest we can't afford to water. Let's go with the Wetland Restoration.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"It warms my heart to see us all in agreement. Choosing a path that respects the water and the land, while ensuring we can truly care for it, is the kindest thing we can do.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"It is the most sustainable option. It addresses the environmental crisis, utilizes our existing volunteer strengths, and avoids the high-maintenance pitfalls of the other plans. I fully support the Wetland Restoration.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"It's rare we agree this quickly, but the logic is sound. D solves the drainage, mitigates the heat, and avoids the maintenance traps of A and B. It's the only plan that actually functions. I vote D.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Minato,,I vote for D. It seems like the best way to help the park and the people who use it without taking too many risks.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,I'm voting for D as well! It's the only one that doesn't look like a financial black hole in the making. Let's get this signed off before the budget changes again!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I shall also cast my vote for D. It is a gentle solution that honors the land and ensures a lasting legacy for all who visit.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I vote for D. It is the only candidate that balances the physical needs of the site with our actual operational capacity and volunteer resources.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I've already stated my position. The evidence is clear, the logic is consistent, and the consensus is absolute. I vote D.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm glad we could all agree on a plan that helps the park. I'm happy to support the Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
